quran[14]{c,v,t}:
  20,38,"when We inspired to your mother that which was inspired, (saying:)"
  20,39,"‘Put him in the chest, then place it into the river. Then the river will throw him on the shore. An enemy of Mine and an enemy of his (i.e. Pharoah) shall pick him up (from there).’ And I blessed you with (an exceptional) love from Me that you might be brought up under My (caring) eyes."
  20,40,"When your sister walked up (to Pharaoh’s family) and said: ‘Shall I direct you to someone who can nurse him?’ Then We brought you back to your mother, that her eyes might be cooled, and she should not grieve. Later, you killed a man (unintentionally), but We saved you from sorrow. Then We tried you with various trials. Then, you stayed among the people of Madyan (Midian) for years. Then you came (here) as ordained, O Musa (Moses)!"
  20,41,I have chosen you for Myself (i.e. the task of Messengership).
  20,42,"Go ahead, you and your brother (Aaron), with My Signs and do not tire in remembering Me."
  20,43,"Go, both of you, to Pharaoh. Indeed, he has rebelled."
  20,44,Speak to him a gentle word. Perhaps he may accept admonition or fear (My wrath).’
  20,45,"Both of them said: ‘Our Lord! Indeed, we fear that he will torture us or become (more) rebellious.’"
  20,46,"He said: ‘Do not fear. Indeed, I am with you both; I hear and I see."
  20,47,"So both of you go to him and say: “Indeed we are two messengers of your Lord. Therefore, let the Children of Israel go with us. And do not persecute them (anymore). Indeed, We have brought you a sign from your Lord. Peace be upon him who follows guidance!"
  20,48,"Indeed, it has been revealed to us that punishment will surely come upon him who rejects (the truth) and turns his back (on us).”’"
  20,49,He (Pharaoh) said: ‘Who is the Lord of you both? O Musa (Moses)!’
  20,50,He (Moses) said: ‘Our Lord is He Who gave everything its distinctive form and then guided it (according to its potential).’
  20,51,He (Pharaoh) said: ‘What about the previous generations?’
